Experiment No.: 1
 Aim: To Study Various Communication Devices and Their Roles at Different Layers
Objectives
After completing this experiment, students will be able to:
● Identify various networking devices.
● Understand the working principle of each device.
● Classify devices according to the OSI layers.
● Differentiate between networking devices based on their functionality.
● Understand real-world applications of networking devices.
Apparatus / Requirements
● Computer System
● Internet Connection
● Cisco Packet Tracer (Optional)
● Networking Devices (if available)
● LAN Cable (RJ-45)
● Wi-Fi Router
● Switch
● Hub
Theory
Communication devices are hardware components that facilitate communication between
computers and networks. These devices operate at different layers of the OSI Reference Model.
Device OSI Layer Function
Hub Physical Layer (Layer 1) Broadcasts incoming data to all connected
devices without filtering.
Repeater Physical Layer (Layer 1) Regenerates and amplifies weak signals to
extend transmission distance.
Modem Physical Layer (Layer 1) Converts digital signals into analog signals and
vice versa for Internet connectivity.
Switch Data Link Layer (Layer 2) Forwards data frames using MAC addresses,
reducing collisions and improving efficiency.
Bridge Data Link Layer (Layer 2) Connects and filters traffic between two LAN
segments based on MAC addresses.
Wireless Access
Point (WAP) Data Link Layer (Layer 2) Provides wireless connectivity for devices to join
a LAN.
