Device OSI Layer Function
Router Network Layer (Layer 3) Routes packets between different networks using
IP addresses.
Gateway Layers 4–7 Connects networks using different protocols and
performs protocol conversion.
Firewall Network/Transport Layer Filters incoming and outgoing traffic to protect
the network from unauthorized access.
OSI Layer Mapping
OSI Layer Devices
Layer 7 – Application Gateway
Layer 6 – Presentation Gateway
Layer 5 – Session Gateway
Layer 4 – Transport Firewall, Gateway
Layer 3 – Network Router
Layer 2 – Data Link Switch, Bridge, Wireless Access Point
Layer 1 – Physical Hub, Repeater, Modem
Procedure-
Study of Functions
1. Study the working principle of:
o Hub
o Switch
o Router
o Bridge
o Repeater
o Modem
2. Identify the OSI layer at which each device operates.
3. Compare their functions.
Result
The communication devices were successfully studied, and their respective roles at different
layers of the OSI model were understood.
